# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# This is not cosmetic, it is a correctness requirement. The vendored parser
# must stay byte-identical to its pinned upstream commit, and
# scripts/check_upstream_parity.py compares bytes. Git's default core.autocrlf
# on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which would make every Windows
# clone report spurious drift on a file nobody touched.
#
# The upstream flagship uses the same single line, for the same class of reason.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the one file whose exact bytes are load-bearing. Even if
# the line above were removed, git will not touch this file's line endings.
netverify/parsers/upstream.py -text

